From 519b410f4fe14cf4a9af8d0f714134a6c202591f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gowtham Suresh Kumar <gowtham.sureshkumar@arm.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 14:48:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Enable SHA3 acceleration for Neoverse N3/V3

Mark Arm Neoverse N3 and V3 as platforms where the SHA3 accelerated
Keccak path is worth using. This enables the optimized SHA3/SHAKE
implementation on these cores, providing better performance.
Behaviour is unchanged on platforms without Armv8.2-A FEAT_SHA3 support.

Original-Commit: 26f45c65a68e "Enable SHA3 acceleration for Neoverse N3/V3"
Original-PR: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33057
Signed-off-by: Gowtham Suresh Kumar <gowtham.sureshkumar@arm.com>
Reviewed-by: Tom Cosgrove <tom.cosgrove@arm.com>
Reviewed-by: Eugene Syromiatnikov <esyr@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Tomas Mraz <tomas@openssl.foundation>
Reviewed-by: Matt Caswell <matt@openssl.foundation>
Merge-date: Fri Oct 30 04:02:03 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33058
(cherry picked from commit 93e0305e50e4860ca1d667c2db8d56d091bf2963)
---
 crypto/armcap.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/crypto/armcap.c b/crypto/armcap.c
index 11ed4abb37b0..3707cfafe7a1 100644
--- a/crypto/armcap.c
+++ b/crypto/armcap.c
@@ -444,7 +444,9 @@ void OPENSSL_cpuid_setup(void)
             || MIDR_IS_CPU_MODEL(OPENSSL_arm_midr, ARM_CPU_IMP_APPLE, APPLE_CPU_PART_M2_AVALANCHE_PRO)
             || MIDR_IS_CPU_MODEL(OPENSSL_arm_midr, ARM_CPU_IMP_APPLE, APPLE_CPU_PART_M2_BLIZZARD_PRO)
             || MIDR_IS_CPU_MODEL(OPENSSL_arm_midr, ARM_CPU_IMP_APPLE, APPLE_CPU_PART_M2_AVALANCHE_MAX)
-            || MIDR_IS_CPU_MODEL(OPENSSL_arm_midr, ARM_CPU_IMP_APPLE, APPLE_CPU_PART_M2_BLIZZARD_MAX)))
+            || MIDR_IS_CPU_MODEL(OPENSSL_arm_midr, ARM_CPU_IMP_APPLE, APPLE_CPU_PART_M2_BLIZZARD_MAX)
+            || MIDR_IS_CPU_MODEL(OPENSSL_arm_midr, ARM_CPU_IMP_ARM, ARM_CPU_PART_N3)
+            || MIDR_IS_CPU_MODEL(OPENSSL_arm_midr, ARM_CPU_IMP_ARM, ARM_CPU_PART_V3)))
         OPENSSL_armcap_P |= ARMV8_HAVE_SHA3_AND_WORTH_USING;
 #endif
 }
